1
00:03:31,111 --> 00:03:37,111
There's nothing like your first piece.

2
00:07:02,222 --> 00:07:08,222
American Pie is a comedy, romance film directed by Paul Weitz.

3
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:39,333
At a high-school party, four friends find that losing their
collective virginity isn't as easy as they had thought.

4
00:14:04,444 --> 00:14:10,444
But they still believe that they need to do so before college.

5
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:41,555
To motivate themselves, they enter a pact to all "score" by their senior prom.

6
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
Jim Levenstein, played by Jason Biggs.

7
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:43,777
Chris 'Oz' Ostreicher, played by Chris Klein.

8
00:28:08,888 --> 00:28:14,888
Kevin Meyers, played by Thomas Ian Nicholas.

9
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Michelle Flaherty, played by Alyson Hannigan.

10
00:35:11,111 --> 00:35:17,111
Nadia, played by Shannon Elizabeth.

11
00:38:42,222 --> 00:38:48,222
Victoria 'Vicky' Lathum, played by Tara Reid.

12
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
American Pie is a 1999 American coming-of-age teen sex comedy film
directed and co-produced by Paul Weitz and written by Adam Herz.

13
00:45:44,444 --> 00:45:50,444
The film's main ensemble cast includes Jason Biggs, Chris Klein, Alyson Hannigan, Natasha Lyonne, Thomas Ian Nicholas, Tara Reid, Mena Suvari, Eddie
Kaye Thomas, and Seann William Scott, with Eugene Levy, Shannon Elizabeth, Chris Owen, and Jennifer Coolidge in notable supporting roles.

14
00:49:15,555 --> 00:49:21,555
The story follows a group of high school classmates who make a
pact to lose their virginity before they graduate.

15
00:52:46,666 --> 00:52:52,666
After the success of Wes Craven's horror teen film Scream (1996), Herz began developing the script for American Pie, originally titled
Untitled Teenage Sex Comedy That Can Be Made For Under $10 Million That Most Readers Will Probably Hate But I Think You Will Love.

16
00:56:17,777 --> 00:56:23,777
A bidding war between major film studios ensued, and
Universal Pictures won the film's rights in 1998.

17
00:59:48,888 --> 00:59:54,888
First-time directors Chris and Paul Weitz were attached as
directors for the film, although only Paul was credited.

18
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Under a new title of Great Falls, filming took
place from July to September 1998.

19
01:06:51,111 --> 01:06:57,111
The picture originally received an NC-17 rating from the Motion Picture
Association of America (MPAA); edits were made to secure an R rating.

20
01:10:22,222 --> 01:10:28,222
The film's title was later changed to American Pie.

21
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
Released theatrically by Universal Pictures on July 9, 1999, in the United States, American Pie initially received
mixed reviews from critics, who were polarized on the raunchy humor but praised the performances.

22
01:17:24,444 --> 01:17:30,444
Nonetheless, the film was a box office success, grossing
$235.5 million worldwide on a $10 million budget.

23
01:20:55,555 --> 01:21:01,555
American Pie revived the teen sex comedy genre for the late 1990s.

24
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
The film's success also spawned a franchise, including three theatrical sequels American Pie 2, American Wedding, and American Reunion, and five
direct-to-video film series American Pie Presents, consisting of Band Camp, The Naked Mile, Beta House, The Book of Love, and Girls' Rules.

25
01:27:57,777 --> 01:28:03,777
The film explores themes of innocence, graduation, loss of
virginity, coming of age, high school student.

26
01:31:28,888 --> 01:31:34,888
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
